\label{Th1}  The space of continuous functions defined on $[0,T],$ whose R-L fractional derivative of order $\beta,$ $0<\beta<1$ are continuous on  $[0,T]$ is a Banach space when endowed with the following norm:
	\begin{align*}
	||\omega||_{\beta}=||\omega||_{\infty}+||D^{\beta}\omega||_{\infty},
	\end{align*}
	where $||.||_{\infty}$ is the supremum norm defined on the class of continuous functions. 	This space will be denoted by $C^{\beta}([0,T]).$

