Consider the special case, $\rho= x_1/x_2$ where $x_{1,2}$ are randomly sampled from Weibull distribution $\tilde{P}(x_i;k,l)$ with same divergent power $k$ and $l$, the result is not related to overall scale.
	\begin{align}
		P(\rho)&= \int_0^\infty \tilde{P}(x_1)\tilde{P}(x_2)\delta\left(\rho-\frac{x_1}{x_2}\right){\rm{d}}x_1{\rm{d}}x_2\nonumber\\
		&=\frac{k \rho^{-1+k}}{(1+\rho^k)^2}\overset{\rho\to 0}{\propto}\rho^{-1+k}\;,
	\end{align}
which gives us  
\begin{equation}
k_\rho=k.
\end{equation}

