The space of possible real Hamiltonians $H_\l$ describing the $T\overline T$ spectrum can then be spanned by the operators
\begin{align}
    \label{unitary transformation}
    H_\lambda = e^{-\lambda X_\lambda} \tilde H_\lambda e^{\lambda X_\lambda}~,
\end{align}
where $X_\lambda$ is some anti-unitary operator. Since the $T\overline T$ deformation acts trivially on the undeformed momentum, we will also need to require that
\begin{align}
    P = e^{-\lambda X_\lambda}Pe^{\lambda X_\lambda},
\end{align}
implying $[P, X_\lambda] = 0$. It also follows that $[H_\lambda, P] = 0$.

