In early data analysis applications, cross-correlated noise is likely
to produce considerable spurious contributions to the integral
(\ref{eq:CCstat}).  A useful diagnostic tool will thus be the
\emph{cross-correlation spectrum}
\begin{equation}
  \label{eq:CCspec}
  Y(f)
  = {\widetilde{h}_1^*(f)}\, {\widetilde{Q}(f)}\,
  {\widetilde{h}_2(f)}
\ ,
\end{equation}
which is simply the integrand of (\ref{eq:CCstat}); this may enable us
to see directly the impact of these cross-correlated noise sources on
the cross-correlation statistic.

